00:22:58.140 --> 00:23:00.370
that's too frightening so we have to push it out again.

556
00:23:00.370 --> 00:23:02.190
Yeah, that's fascinating.

557
00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:05.110
That's so interesting, why do you think we do that?

558
00:23:06.043 --> 00:23:11.043
I mean, because the fear of the unknown exceeds

559
00:23:12.180 --> 00:23:14.820
like the discomfort of the current.

560
00:23:14.820 --> 00:23:17.460
I think people are afraid of what would happen

561
00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:19.410
if they actually put themselves on the line

562
00:23:19.410 --> 00:23:24.410
and there's a certain comfort level in just continuing along

563
00:23:25.500 --> 00:23:28.140
the current path and there's a level

564
00:23:28.140 --> 00:23:32.400
of emotional self sabotage that I think certain people have.

565
00:23:32.400 --> 00:23:33.480
I know what that feels like.

566
00:23:33.480 --> 00:23:36.333
Yeah, 1000%, I love that.

567
00:23:37.740 --> 00:23:41.250
So yeah, it was after eight years, we were doing the same.

568
00:23:41.250 --> 00:23:42.660
It was like, oh, well, we'll do this-

569
00:23:42.660 --> 00:23:43.493
Eight years.

570
00:23:43.493 --> 00:23:44.670
Yeah, we'll do this when.

571
00:23:44.670 --> 00:23:46.440
I'll speak up when.

572
00:23:46.440 --> 00:23:48.450
When we have enough money then I'll be happy.

573
00:23:48.450 --> 00:23:51.270
When my husband feels successful, he'll be happy

574
00:23:51.270 --> 00:23:52.290
so then I'll be happy.

575
00:23:52.290 --> 00:23:54.720
And so there was always the when and eventually

576
00:23:54.720 --> 00:23:57.510
what happened was we would ended up chasing money.

577
00:23:57.510 --> 00:23:59.400
And to me, I'd always made a commitment.

578
00:23:59.400 --> 00:24:01.290
Like I was okay with actually being unhappy.

579
00:24:01.290 --> 00:24:04.140
I wasn't okay with my relationship breaking.

580
00:24:04.140 --> 00:24:07.170
And when I started to see that Tom's unhappiness

