582
00:24:10.740 --> 00:24:13.350
it almost gave me the jolt I needed to say,

583
00:24:13.350 --> 00:24:15.690
hey, I don't care about money

584
00:24:15.690 --> 00:24:18.270
like what the hell are we doing right now?

585
00:24:18.270 --> 00:24:20.730
I've lost my husband, you don't seem happy.

586
00:24:20.730 --> 00:24:23.550
I've lost who you are, your personality, I'm not happy.

587
00:24:23.550 --> 00:24:25.260
So what on earth are we doing this for?

588
00:24:25.260 --> 00:24:28.170
So let's just reassess what our life should look like.

589
00:24:28.170 --> 00:24:30.000
And of course, surprise, surprise,

590
00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.260
we tried to run away from the problem.

591
00:24:31.260 --> 00:24:32.550
So it was like, oh, well, we'll just quit

592
00:24:32.550 --> 00:24:33.480
and move countries.

593
00:24:33.480 --> 00:24:35.430
That should be fine, we'll go to Greece and we'll just write

594
00:24:35.430 --> 00:24:36.453
and we'll be happy.

595
00:24:37.440 --> 00:24:41.130
And so in that process, Tom had these two business partners.

596
00:24:41.130 --> 00:24:42.057
So for the eight years,

597
00:24:42.057 --> 00:24:44.070
they were trying to make enough money, build a company

598
00:24:44.070 --> 00:24:46.320
and so eventually he's like, all right, I'll go in and quit.

599
00:24:46.320 --> 00:24:49.950
And on paper, we had earned a couple of million dollars

600
00:24:49.950 --> 00:24:51.990
but we were both of the mindsets if you don't cross

601
00:24:51.990 --> 00:24:53.640
the finish line, you don't get the payout.

602
00:24:53.640 --> 00:24:55.650
We weren't willing to cross the finish line.

603
00:24:55.650 --> 00:24:57.540
And so that was one of those moments where it's like,

604
00:24:57.540 --> 00:24:59.010
oh, money doesn't buy happiness.

605
00:24:59.010 --> 00:24:59.850
Well, they kept saying

606
00:24:59.850 --> 00:25:01.137
they were gonna sell the company, right?

607
00:25:01.137 --> 00:25:03.870
And that kinda dragged along and kept you in it

608
00:25:03.870 --> 00:25:07.380
longer than you wanted to be because that never happened.

609
00:25:07.380 --> 00:25:09.780
And it wasn't until, didn't didn't you guys decide,

610
00:25:09.780 --> 00:25:11.940
okay, Tom's gonna quit, he goes into quit

611
00:25:11.940 --> 00:25:13.830
and then it was one more thing like, okay,

612
00:25:13.830 --> 00:25:15.515
well now we're gonna reconfigure.

613
00:25:15.515 --> 00:25:18.150
Six more months and then we're gonna change the way

614
00:25:18.150 --> 00:25:20.280
we're doing things and we're gonna try this other thing.

615
00:25:20.280 --> 00:25:22.200
Yeah, the difference in that situation,

616
00:25:22.200 --> 00:25:24.270
so after the eight years, we finally had the talk,

617
00:25:24.270 --> 00:25:25.620
this isn't good for our relationship,

618
00:25:25.620 --> 00:25:27.780
what's the point in success if you're not happy?

619
00:25:27.780 --> 00:25:29.010
We're chasing money.

620
00:25:29.010 --> 00:25:31.110
On paper, now got a couple of million dollars

621
00:25:31.110 --> 00:25:33.030
that we've helped build this other company

622
00:25:33.030 --> 00:25:35.730
and yet we are the most unhappy we've ever been.

623
00:25:35.730 --> 00:25:39.090
So the change was to go in and quit and finally he did.

624
00:25:39.090 --> 00:25:41.010
And that was the pivot where he went in,

625
00:25:41.010 --> 00:25:42.870
told his business partners and they admitted

626
00:25:42.870 --> 00:25:44.550
they were unhappy too.

627
00:25:44.550 --> 00:25:46.830
And so in that, they said, okay,

628
00:25:46.830 --> 00:25:49.080
now we've at least been honest with each other,

629
00:25:49.080 --> 00:25:52.650
we need to come up with a path and a strategy to get out.

