1748
01:11:43.260 --> 01:11:48.240
So I sat back and I came up with a plan and the plan was,

1749
01:11:48.240 --> 01:11:50.340
the strategy was listen to your negative voice

1750
01:11:50.340 --> 01:11:52.080
'cause the negative voice used to hold me back.

1751
01:11:52.080 --> 01:11:53.910
But I was like, what if just like your husband,

1752
01:11:53.910 --> 01:11:54.870
is trying to warn you something?

1753
01:11:54.870 --> 01:11:56.400
He's trying to give you a signal?

1754
01:11:56.400 --> 01:11:58.740
So I sat back and I said, what is it trying to warn you?

1755
01:11:58.740 --> 01:12:00.060
Okay, just listen to it.

1756
01:12:00.060 --> 01:12:02.520
It's saying like, oh my God, you're so fearful,

1757
01:12:02.520 --> 01:12:03.420
you can't even say yes.

1758
01:12:03.420 --> 01:12:05.910
So I was like, okay, I can't even say yes to a speaking gig,

1759
01:12:05.910 --> 01:12:07.590
how do I overcome that?

1760
01:12:07.590 --> 01:12:09.687
Oh, hang on, they actually reach out to my team first

1761
01:12:09.687 --> 01:12:11.460
and it's my team that tell me.

1762
01:12:11.460 --> 01:12:12.990
So I'm just gonna tell my team next time,

1763
01:12:12.990 --> 01:12:15.390
just say yes, don't check with me, okay, great.

1764
01:12:15.390 --> 01:12:17.537
Now I've overcome that fear, what's the next thing

1765
01:12:17.537 --> 01:12:20.482
the voice in your head is saying, you're not as good as Tom.

1766
01:12:20.482 --> 01:12:22.920
You're gonna go on stage, Lisa, you're gonna bomb.

1767
01:12:22.920 --> 01:12:24.720
All right, so maybe she's right.

1768
01:12:24.720 --> 01:12:27.330
This critic in my head, maybe she's right,

1769
01:12:27.330 --> 01:12:28.410
maybe she can coach me.

1770
01:12:28.410 --> 01:12:31.350
So I was like, all right, turn the critic into a coach,

1771
01:12:31.350 --> 01:12:32.430
I can do that.

1772
01:12:32.430 --> 01:12:33.450
What is she saying?

1773
01:12:33.450 --> 01:12:35.820
Get prepared, that's what she's saying.

1774
01:12:35.820 --> 01:12:37.530
So I'm like, oh, she wants me to prepare.

1775
01:12:37.530 --> 01:12:38.363
Okay, great.

1776
01:12:38.363 --> 01:12:40.380
So now I just lay out, how am I gonna prepare?

1777
01:12:40.380 --> 01:12:41.640
What does that look like?

1778
01:12:41.640 --> 01:12:44.220
Because the voice in my head is very scared.

1779
01:12:44.220 --> 01:12:46.800
So number one, I'm going to have someone coach me

1780
01:12:46.800 --> 01:12:47.970
on how to do a speaking gig

1781
01:12:47.970 --> 01:12:49.080
'cause I've never done it before.

1782
01:12:49.080 --> 01:12:51.630
Who do I know my husband, great, let me book time with him.

1783
01:12:51.630 --> 01:12:53.550
Number two, how am I gonna read it out loud?

1784
01:12:53.550 --> 01:12:55.590
Okay, I'm gonna read it to him, that's one person.

1785
01:12:55.590 --> 01:12:57.840
Then I'm gonna read it to my team, that's 20 people.

1786
01:12:57.840 --> 01:13:00.420
And I literally sat there and wrote a game plan

1787
01:13:00.420 --> 01:13:02.680
so that every time I woke up the next day,

1788
01:13:02.680 --> 01:13:03.780
I was like, what do I do today?

1789
01:13:03.780 --> 01:13:05.460
It wasn't, how do I feel,

1790
01:13:05.460 --> 01:13:07.039
it was, what do I do?

1791
01:13:07.039 --> 01:13:11.040
And so, that was how I started to process the fear,

1792
01:13:11.040 --> 01:13:15.210
not listening to it, telling my ego to calm the hell down

1793
01:13:15.210 --> 01:13:16.443
and then still show up.

1794
01:13:17.460 --> 01:13:22.460
Yeah, it's a function of preparation but self-esteem

1795
01:13:22.740 --> 01:13:27.740
being the driver of confidence and self-esteem being driven

1796
01:13:28.080 --> 01:13:31.170
by performing esteemable acts on behalf of others

1797
01:13:31.170 --> 01:13:35.430
and yourself, the path really is setting up

1798
01:13:35.430 --> 01:13:38.970
these stepping stones along the way such that

1799
01:13:38.970 --> 01:13:41.550
when you get to that stage or you're gonna drop in

1800
01:13:41.550 --> 01:13:44.100
on that wave or you're gonna, whatever it is,

1801
01:13:44.100 --> 01:13:47.975
walk into the gym, you've already done enough legwork

1802
01:13:47.975 --> 01:13:52.740
in lower stakes environments that next step to the thing

1803
01:13:52.740 --> 01:13:55.530
that once scared you doesn't feel as intimidating

1804
01:13:55.530 --> 01:13:58.740
as it once was so practicing your speech in the mirror,

1805
01:13:58.740 --> 01:14:01.380
sharing it with a friend, being open to feedback,

1806
01:14:01.380 --> 01:14:03.870
doing it in front of two people and then three people

1807
01:14:03.870 --> 01:14:06.450
and then memorizing it and then doing it to a camera

1808
01:14:06.450 --> 01:14:09.870
and then having the gall to watch yourself on like

1809
01:14:09.870 --> 01:14:14.290
all of those things are very low stakes but are so important

1810
01:14:15.300 --> 01:14:17.340
in terms of the ramp up.

1811
01:14:17.340 --> 01:14:19.920
So that way it's not like, oh, I'm going from nothing

1812
01:14:19.920 --> 01:14:22.650
to walking on this TEDx stage, right?

1813
01:14:22.650 --> 01:14:27.570
Like there's a whole battery of interim stages

1814
01:14:27.570 --> 01:14:28.980
that prepare you.

1815
01:14:28.980 --> 01:14:29.850
Yeah, exactly.

1816
01:14:29.850 --> 01:14:32.520
And then even just, you said the walking on the stage,

1817
01:14:32.520 --> 01:14:34.410
that was so petrifying to me 'cause even

1818
01:14:34.410 --> 01:14:36.407
with all the preparation, I was like,

1819
01:14:36.407 --> 01:14:38.580
how do you actually walk on stage?

1820
01:14:38.580 --> 01:14:40.800
Like when you are as scared as I was, I was like,

1821
01:14:40.800 --> 01:14:44.220
I may be prepared but I worried as soon as I got

1822
01:14:44.220 --> 01:14:46.980
to the steps and I saw the audience, I would freeze.

1823
01:14:46.980 --> 01:14:50.070
So again, I allowed the voice in my head to talk and say,

1824
01:14:50.070 --> 01:14:52.170
Lisa, you don't wanna freeze like, oh my God,

1825
01:14:52.170 --> 01:14:53.461
people will laugh at you.

1826
01:14:53.461 --> 01:14:55.410
And I was like, okay, what tools do I have

1827
01:14:55.410 --> 01:14:58.110
to my ability that I can use to help me get on stage?

1828
01:14:58.110 --> 01:15:00.630
Because to me, my goal wasn't to be amazing on stage,

1829
01:15:00.630 --> 01:15:02.940
it was like, just actually do it.

1830
01:15:02.940 --> 01:15:04.620
You said that you were going to and do it.

1831
01:15:04.620 --> 01:15:06.780
That becomes the self-esteem part, right?

1832
01:15:06.780 --> 01:15:08.610
It's like I was holding my self-esteem to,

1833
01:15:08.610 --> 01:15:10.800
am I the person that shows up?

1834
01:15:10.800 --> 01:15:13.500
And so even if I bomb, at least I did it

1835
01:15:13.500 --> 01:15:14.547
and that's why I kept telling myself

1836
01:15:14.547 --> 01:15:16.813
but how long do I just show up on stage?

1837
01:15:16.813 --> 01:15:20.190
And so I just literally sat there and I was like,

1838
01:15:20.190 --> 01:15:22.620
okay, what are the tools that I can use

1839
01:15:22.620 --> 01:15:23.790
to help encourage me?

1840
01:15:23.790 --> 01:15:26.580
And I thought about the kids, do you have kids?

1841
01:15:26.580 --> 01:15:27.510
Hm-hm.

1842
01:15:27.510 --> 01:15:29.340
Did you ever give them a cape when they were kids?

1843
01:15:29.340 --> 01:15:30.173
I don't think so.

1844
01:15:30.173 --> 01:15:32.913
No, capes weren't my kids' things.

1845
01:15:32.913 --> 01:15:34.380
Okay, have you ever given a cape to a kid

1846
01:15:34.380 --> 01:15:35.520
and seen what they do?

1847
01:15:35.520 --> 01:15:36.820
Sure, I have seen that, of course.

1848
01:15:36.820 --> 01:15:38.487
Okay, they put their fist in the air, right?

1849
01:15:38.487 --> 01:15:40.830
And they're like, act like Superman or like,

1850
01:15:40.830 --> 01:15:42.870
I love Wonder Woman.

1851
01:15:42.870 --> 01:15:44.700
And I was like the power of clothes,

1852
01:15:44.700 --> 01:15:47.760
the power of something like that to a kid takes them

1853
01:15:47.760 --> 01:15:50.250
from being the kid to then actually them believing

1854
01:15:50.250 --> 01:15:51.570
they're a superhero.

1855
01:15:51.570 --> 01:15:53.460
So why don't we do that as adults?

1856
01:15:53.460 --> 01:15:56.132
It's such a great like mind hack.

1857
01:15:56.132 --> 01:15:58.427
And so I was like, what could that be for me?

1858
01:15:58.427 --> 01:16:00.540
And so I love Wonder Woman and so I was like,

1859
01:16:00.540 --> 01:16:02.547
oh, what if I got a Wonder Woman necklace?

1860
01:16:02.547 --> 01:16:03.505
So you see it here.

1861
01:16:03.505 --> 01:16:04.338
Yeah, yeah.

1862
01:16:04.338 --> 01:16:06.600
And so what I started to do is like, okay,

1863
01:16:06.600 --> 01:16:09.518
I've got my little item that is like the self signaling part

1864
01:16:09.518 --> 01:16:13.290
but I also know that you need to create a habit.

1865
01:16:13.290 --> 01:16:15.180
So every time I put it on, I was like,

1866
01:16:15.180 --> 01:16:18.360
well, how do I reinforce that I feel like Wonder Woman

1867
01:16:18.360 --> 01:16:19.440
when I put it on?

1868
01:16:19.440 --> 01:16:21.994
So I came up with a strategy that for about a month

1869
01:16:21.994 --> 01:16:23.850
'cause they say 30 days is what you have to do, right?

1870
01:16:23.850 --> 01:16:24.930
To create a habit.

1871
01:16:24.930 --> 01:16:27.180
So I kept putting on every day for 30 days

1872
01:16:27.180 --> 01:16:29.130
and every day I put it on, I was like, you're a badass

1873
01:16:29.130 --> 01:16:30.090
like Wonder Woman.

1874
01:16:30.090 --> 01:16:31.770
You're a badass like Wonder Woman.

1875
01:16:31.770 --> 01:16:34.320
And so, what I was doing was repeating that enough

1876
01:16:34.320 --> 01:16:35.640
that I was creating a habit.

1877
01:16:35.640 --> 01:16:37.200
So that before I got on stage,

1878
01:16:37.200 --> 01:16:38.670
I put on my Wonder Woman, necklace.

1879
01:16:38.670 --> 01:16:40.080
I have my hair braided.

1880
01:16:40.080 --> 01:16:42.933
I have on these big watch and cuffs and stuff-

1881
01:16:42.933 --> 01:16:46.713
That watch is gigantic by the way,

1882
01:16:46.713 --> 01:16:48.176
which is that way on your wrist.

1883
01:16:48.176 --> 01:16:50.843
I know, people are just like that watch is wearing you.

1884
01:16:51.791 --> 01:16:53.520
But all of these things are very deliberate,

1885
01:16:53.520 --> 01:16:55.800
I don't do this by accident because I can get

1886
01:16:55.800 --> 01:16:58.890
in my own head and so I literally think of ways

1887
01:16:58.890 --> 01:17:01.950
that I can overcome the way that I naturally am.

1888
01:17:01.950 --> 01:17:03.900
I don't beat myself up by having the negative thoughts,

1889
01:17:03.900 --> 01:17:06.360
I don't beat myself up fearing going on stage,

1890
01:17:06.360 --> 01:17:08.310
I just don't allow that to stop me.

1891
01:17:08.310 --> 01:17:13.310
Yeah it reminds me of this idea of the alter ego

1892
01:17:14.910 --> 01:17:18.540
like David Goggins becomes Goggins or James Lawrence

1893
01:17:18.540 --> 01:17:20.670
becomes the Iron cowboy.

1894
01:17:20.670 --> 01:17:25.410
And it's a way of putting on that sort of superhero costume

1895
01:17:25.410 --> 01:17:28.620
in whatever way, shape or form serves you.

1896
01:17:28.620 --> 01:17:33.600
It's also the idea that this guy, Todd Herman,

1897
01:17:33.600 --> 01:17:35.790
who's been on my podcast before who wrote a whole book

1898
01:17:35.790 --> 01:17:37.830
about this, "The Alter Ego Effect".

1899
01:17:37.830 --> 01:17:38.703
You probably-

1900
01:17:38.703 --> 01:17:39.813
I haven't actually read it but I know it's from him.

1901
01:17:39.813 --> 01:17:42.030
Yeah I mean, that's like right up the alley

1902
01:17:42.030 --> 01:17:44.970
of exactly what you're talking about which is creating

1903
01:17:44.970 --> 01:17:47.280
a little bit of distance between your fear

1904
01:17:47.280 --> 01:17:50.490
and what you're trying to achieve by armoring yourself

1905
01:17:50.490 --> 01:17:53.250
in something that allows you to kinda transcend

1906
01:17:53.250 --> 01:17:56.190
those insecurities and step into something greater.

1907
01:17:56.190 --> 01:17:59.130
Yeah, I love that and also I actually feel

1908
01:17:59.130 --> 01:18:00.630
a chemical change.

1909
01:18:00.630 --> 01:18:03.900
Like I start to feel more powerful as I like kinda suit up,

1910
01:18:03.900 --> 01:18:06.720
as I do my hair, as I put my jewelry on.

1911
01:18:06.720 --> 01:18:09.750
And so that power of like having these symbols,

1912
01:18:09.750 --> 01:18:12.180
I also find the beauty and the reverse.

1913
01:18:12.180 --> 01:18:16.050
So some days I'm going really hard for the business,

1914
01:18:16.050 --> 01:18:17.100
it's a grind.

1915
01:18:17.100 --> 01:18:19.530
It's you're facing problems all day, every day

1916
01:18:19.530 --> 01:18:22.260
and you're having people and just feel overwhelmed,

1917
01:18:22.260 --> 01:18:26.070
in those moments, I feel very hard like I can feel myself

1918
01:18:26.070 --> 01:18:27.717
toughen and I've got gut issues.

1919
01:18:27.717 --> 01:18:31.620
And so I recognize having massive like anxiety

1920
01:18:31.620 --> 01:18:34.230
or like stressful days isn't good for my health.

1921
01:18:34.230 --> 01:18:37.410
And so what tools am I going to use in moments of that?

1922
01:18:37.410 --> 01:18:39.480
And so usually it's like, I'll get a hug for my husband,

1923
01:18:39.480 --> 01:18:40.620
he normally does it.

1924
01:18:40.620 --> 01:18:44.460
The problem is sometimes when you're that elevated

1925
01:18:44.460 --> 01:18:47.280
in like emotion or you're angry or you're just like

1926
01:18:47.280 --> 01:18:51.510
really hard that day, a hug isn't something that you need.

1927
01:18:51.510 --> 01:18:53.880
And so I was like, oh, what if I do the opposite?

1928
01:18:53.880 --> 01:18:57.060
What if I undo myself, so what if I undo my braids,

1929
01:18:57.060 --> 01:19:00.180
my jewelry put on something that makes me feel soft.

1930
01:19:00.180 --> 01:19:02.130
So I have these surprise, surprise,

1931
01:19:02.130 --> 01:19:06.030
Wonder Woman fluffy pajamas and I unwind when I'm trying

1932
01:19:06.030 --> 01:19:08.460
to change the chemicals in my body,

1933
01:19:08.460 --> 01:19:09.870
I know what I can reach for.

1934
01:19:09.870 --> 01:19:12.750
So I take off the jewelry, I take down the hair

1935
01:19:12.750 --> 01:19:15.270
and then I put on something soft that makes me feel soft

1936
01:19:15.270 --> 01:19:17.964
so that I can then embody the softness and then I can go

1937
01:19:17.964 --> 01:19:20.880
get the hug from my husband and then usually eat my dinner.

1938
01:19:20.880 --> 01:19:25.200
But I won't eat my dinner if I'm all tired hard.

1939
01:19:25.200 --> 01:19:28.350
So I need those strategies in order to help me prevent,

1940
01:19:28.350 --> 01:19:29.850
take care of myself.

1941
01:19:29.850 --> 01:19:32.730
And the gut issues are, excuse me,

1942
01:19:32.730 --> 01:19:35.070
like some form of dysbiosis,

1943
01:19:35.070 --> 01:19:36.990
like what is the diagnosis there?

1944
01:19:36.990 --> 01:19:38.472
And there's a whole journey there, yeah.

1945
01:19:38.472 --> 01:19:39.660
Yeah.

1946
01:19:39.660 --> 01:19:42.930
So 10 years as Quest was growing, my identity was tied

1947
01:19:42.930 --> 01:19:45.030
to being the person that always showed up.

1948
01:19:45.030 --> 01:19:47.730
So I was so fearful of slipping backwards

1949
01:19:47.730 --> 01:19:49.650
into being a supportive wife's stay at home

1950
01:19:49.650 --> 01:19:52.140
and because I loved what I was doing at Quest.

1951
01:19:52.140 --> 01:19:54.600
I was just on the grind every day.

1952
01:19:54.600 --> 01:19:57.270
And I thought back then, especially back then,

1953
01:19:57.270 --> 01:19:59.513
I think it was definitely like how many hours do you work?

1954
01:19:59.513 --> 01:20:00.595
Well, how many hours do you work?

1955
01:20:00.595 --> 01:20:02.280
It was like, the pride was in the amount

1956
01:20:02.280 --> 01:20:04.200
of hard work you do.

1957
01:20:04.200 --> 01:20:07.650
And so, at the time I thought of myself as the more hours

1958
01:20:07.650 --> 01:20:09.480
I put in, the more validation I would get,

1959
01:20:09.480 --> 01:20:11.580
the more pats on the back I would get from other people

1960
01:20:11.580 --> 01:20:15.180
'cause I didn't feel good about myself, so I was being like,

1961
01:20:15.180 --> 01:20:18.120
I was thriving off the validation I was getting

1962
01:20:18.120 --> 01:20:19.200
from other people.

1963
01:20:19.200 --> 01:20:21.900
So for 10 years, I stopped all of,

1964
01:20:21.900 --> 01:20:24.390
I draw as like my hobby with art.

1965
01:20:24.390 --> 01:20:27.570
I stopped all of that, I stopped all of my self care.

1966
01:20:27.570 --> 01:20:31.470
I was very negative on myself, very hard on myself.

1967
01:20:31.470 --> 01:20:33.930
I thought sleep was the last thing people needed.

1968
01:20:33.930 --> 01:20:36.210
I also had a very unhealthy relationship growing up

1969
01:20:36.210 --> 01:20:38.580
with food, I saw my mom borderline anorexic

1970
01:20:38.580 --> 01:20:42.033
and then turned into clinically obese.

1971
01:20:42.870 --> 01:20:45.120
And so I had a very unhealthy relationship with food.

1972
01:20:45.120 --> 01:20:47.970
So you put all that together, I started getting sick a lot.

1973
01:20:47.970 --> 01:20:51.390
I didn't realize 70% of your immune system

1974
01:20:51.390 --> 01:20:52.500
is carried in your gut.

1975
01:20:52.500 --> 01:20:56.490
So I was not replenishing my gut with any fats or carbs

1976
01:20:56.490 --> 01:20:57.750
'cause I thought those were bad.

1977
01:20:57.750 --> 01:21:00.960
Doctors were giving me antibiotics and it got to the point

1978
01:21:00.960 --> 01:21:03.120
where I was taking antibiotics probably

1979
01:21:03.120 --> 01:21:04.500
four to five times a year.

1980
01:21:04.500 --> 01:21:05.520
But you do that-

1981
01:21:05.520 --> 01:21:07.908
Of course, just making it worse and worse

1982
01:21:07.908 --> 01:21:11.394
and you're just basically annihilating your whole microbiome

1983
01:21:11.394 --> 01:21:12.518
every time you do that.

1984
01:21:12.518 --> 01:21:15.360
Everything and I was doing that probably,

1985
01:21:15.360 --> 01:21:17.550
started off with an unhealthy relationship with food

1986
01:21:17.550 --> 01:21:19.830
for like, let's say period of 15 years.

1987
01:21:19.830 --> 01:21:23.433
And it became so cliche and it ended up being the best thing

1988
01:21:23.433 --> 01:21:27.210
that ever happened to me but as we're building Quest,

1989
01:21:27.210 --> 01:21:29.670
Tom and I used to take drives around Beverly Hills

1990
01:21:29.670 --> 01:21:30.810
in our really crappy car

1991
01:21:30.810 --> 01:21:32.760
and it was like the moments where we would dream.

1992
01:21:32.760 --> 01:21:33.593
When things were getting very hard,

1993
01:21:33.593 --> 01:21:36.210
we would dream about when Quest got successful,

1994
01:21:36.210 --> 01:21:37.650
